From: HELiX maintainers
Subject: [PATCH v2] rea#62 + rea#63 backports: counter double-zero + hash portability (+ Codex hardening)

Three CodeRabbit / Codex findings on push-review-core.sh (round 3 + round 4,
PR #1506):

- rea#62: LINE_COUNT/FILE_COUNT with `grep -c ... || echo "0"` produce
  "0\n0" when grep exits non-zero on no matches. Misrenders the user-
  facing "Scope: X files changed, Y lines" message. Fix: replace
  `|| echo "0"` with `|| true` + `${VAR:-0}` fallback so a single "0"
  is captured.

- rea#63: PUSH_SHA pipelines `shasum -a 256`, which isn't available on
  Alpine or most distroless images. Silent empty PUSH_SHA disables the
  review cache check with no signal. Fix: portable hasher chain
  (sha256sum -> shasum -> openssl dgst) with Codex-review hardening:

  * openssl form uses `awk '{print $NF}'` without `-r`, so it works on
    BOTH OpenSSL 1.1.x (`(stdin)= <hex>`) and OpenSSL 3.x / LibreSSL
    3.3+ (`<hex> *stdin`). The `-r` flag is unknown on 1.1.x — still
    the default on Debian 11, Ubuntu 20.04, RHEL8, Amazon Linux 2, and
    several Alpine 3.13–3.14 images — and would silently re-introduce
    the empty-PUSH_SHA defect on exactly the distros this patch is
    supposed to rescue.
  * No-hasher branch now emits a stderr WARN so ops can see cache was
    disabled instead of silent-disarming (closes defect F for this
    path).
  * Hex-validation sanity check: if any hasher returned anything other
    than a 64-char lowercase hex digest (broken pipe, partial read,
    unexpected output format), emit WARN and blank PUSH_SHA rather
    than passing a garbage sha into the cache lookup.

Both filed upstream for 0.9.3 (rea#62, rea#63). Drop this patch on next
`rea upgrade` once 0.9.3 lands.

---
 .claude/hooks/_lib/push-review-core.sh | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/hooks/_lib/push-review-core.sh b/.claude/hooks/_lib/push-review-core.sh
--- a/.claude/hooks/_lib/push-review-core.sh
+++ b/.claude/hooks/_lib/push-review-core.sh
@@ -986,7 +986,9 @@
   fi

   local LINE_COUNT
-  LINE_COUNT=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | grep -cE '^\+[^+]|^-[^-]' 2>/dev/null || echo "0")
+  # rea#62 backport (local): `|| echo "0"` on `grep -c` no-match produces "0\n0"
+  LINE_COUNT=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | grep -cE '^\+[^+]|^-[^-]' 2>/dev/null || true)
+  LINE_COUNT="${LINE_COUNT:-0}"

   # ── 7a. Protected-path Codex adversarial review gate ──────────────────────
   # The per-refspec check runs inside the main loop (section 7, above) so
@@ -998,7 +1000,24 @@

   # ── 8. Check review cache ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   local PUSH_SHA
-  PUSH_SHA=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | shasum -a 256 | cut -d' ' -f1 2>/dev/null || echo "")
+  # rea#63 backport (local): `shasum` isn't on Alpine/distroless — try portable chain.
+  # openssl form uses `$NF` (not `-r | $1`) so it works on BOTH OpenSSL 1.1.x
+  # (`(stdin)= <hex>`) and 3.x / LibreSSL 3.3+ (`<hex> *stdin`). `-r` is unknown
+  # on 1.1.x (Debian 11, Ubuntu 20.04, RHEL8, AL2) and would silently return empty.
+  if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    PUSH_SHA=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')
+  elif command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    PUSH_SHA=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | shasum -a 256 | awk '{print $1}')
+  elif command -v openssl >/dev/null 2>&1; then
+    PUSH_SHA=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | openssl dgst -sha256 | awk '{print $NF}')
+  else
+    printf 'push-review: WARN no sha256 hasher found (sha256sum/shasum/openssl); cache disabled\n' >&2
+    PUSH_SHA=""
+  fi
+  if [[ -n "$PUSH_SHA" && ! "$PUSH_SHA" =~ ^[0-9a-f]{64}$ ]]; then
+    printf 'push-review: WARN hasher returned invalid output; cache disabled\n' >&2
+    PUSH_SHA=""
+  fi

   local -a REA_CLI_ARGS
   REA_CLI_ARGS=()
@@ -1054,7 +1073,8 @@

   # ── 9. Block and request review ───────────────────────────────────────────
   local FILE_COUNT
-  FILE_COUNT=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | grep -c '^\+\+\+ ' 2>/dev/null || echo "0")
+  FILE_COUNT=$(printf '%s' "$DIFF_FULL" | grep -c '^\+\+\+ ' 2>/dev/null || true)
+  FILE_COUNT="${FILE_COUNT:-0}"

   {
     printf 'PUSH REVIEW GATE: Review required before pushing\n'
